{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_09_19_graffiti_to_graphify_design", "label": "repo \u2014 replace the graffiti code map with graphify (design spec)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-19-graffiti-to-graphify-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Approved after running the \u00a712 probe; motivated by capability not breakage \u2014 graphify adds community detection, god-nodes, path, explain and affected for free (deterministic Leiden/Louvain, tree-sitter AST) over the same kind of graph graffiti already built."}, {"id": "graffiti", "label": "graffiti (superseded code-map tool)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-19-graffiti-to-graphify-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Worked, but returned only file-level nodes for a Terraform capacity question (0 .tf/.tfvars nodes) versus graphify's 17, and was deleted last (Task 11) only after both verification gates passed, so it remained the control until then."}, {"id": "graphify", "label": "graphify (code-map tool)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-19-graffiti-to-graphify-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Requires the graphifyy[terraform] extra or 30 .tf/2 .hcl/1 .tfvars files (33 of 81 code files) silently contribute nothing to the graph \u2014 it warns rather than fails, so an incomplete map looks complete."}, {"id": "ecs_dynamodb_rps_infra_main_dev", "label": "ecs-dynamodb-rps/infra/main/dev.tfvars", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-19-graffiti-to-graphify-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Commi